infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two ways to author a Transform
  desc Push per chunk and memory stays flat; buffer everything in _flush and a 4GB input costs 4GB and OOMs
  compares
    - label Push as you go
      children
        - label ~3×16KB across a 3-stage pipeline
          desc One highWaterMark buffer per stage, not the whole file
        - label this.push() per chunk in _transform
          desc Emit zero or more outputs, then call cb()
        - label _flush emits only the leftover
          desc A trailer or last partial line, not the dataset
        - label Memory stays flat as input grows
          desc A 4GB input streams in ~48KB of working memory
        - label Backpressure on both sides
          desc 16KB / 16-object highWaterMark per side
    - label Buffer everything in _flush
      children
        - label Holds the entire dataset in RAM
          desc Accumulate all chunks, emit only at the end
        - label 4GB input costs 4GB, then OOMs
          desc The same job that should have cost ~48KB
        - label Defeats streaming silently
          desc Fine on small inputs, fatal on large ones
        - label Crash scales with input size
          desc Passes in staging, dies under production load
        - label The cardinal Transform sin
          desc The whole point is to push as you go
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
